WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.860
An ancient story tells of Job, a
good man who loses his children,

2
00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:07.240
his wealth and his health.

3
00:00:07.290 --> 00:00:10.100
His friends insist he must have sinned.

4
00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:11.650
Are they right?

5
00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:15.470
Centuries later, believers
still ask Job's question,

6
00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:17.730
and give very different answers.

7
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:23.480
Floods, plagues and genocide: and
many believers keep their faith.

8
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:26.870
So what answers do
believers give to suffering?

9
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.270
In this mission, you'll meet
two classic Christian answers,

10
00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.700
from Augustine and Irenaeus,
and the objections to both.

11
00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:38.930
Then you'll read Job's story, see
what believers do in practice,

12
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.040
and weigh up whether their
answers solve the problem.

13
00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.430
Your mission: find out what
answers believers give,

14
00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.680
and whether they work.
